Two defects found and fixed during browser testing, both preserved in the file on disk:
  - frame() originally used requestAnimationFrame alone, which is paused in a background tab and hung the tool forever. It now races rAF against a 50ms timeout so it always continues.
  - show() originally rendered a trailing-space difference invisibly. It now reveals edge whitespace and line breaks as ·, ⇥, ⏎ in the display only, with the convention stated in both the drift note and the report NOTES.